if (!context.getProperty("jsonSlurper")) {
    context.setProperty("jsonSlurper", new groovy.json.JsonSlurper())
}
def jsonSlurper = context.getProperty("jsonSlurper")
```

2. **Batch Operations:**
```groovy
// Instead of multiple API calls, batch them
def ids = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
def results = ids.collect { id ->
    // Process in parallel for performance
    Thread.start {
        // API call
    }
}.collect { it.join() }
```

3. **Lazy Evaluation:**
```groovy
// Use lazy evaluation where possible
def data = new groovy.json.JsonSlurper().parseText(messageExchange.responseContent)
def largeList = data.items.findAll { it.active }
// Process only first 10 if needed
def processed = largeList.take(10).collect { processItem(it) }
```

**Debugging Tips:**

```groovy
