**Dealing with Changing Values in Responses:**

Real-world APIs often return dynamic data that changes with each request—timestamps, generated IDs, random values. Validating these requires special strategies.

**Types of Dynamic Data:**

| Type | Examples | Validation Strategy |
|------|----------|---------------------|
| **Generated IDs** | user_12345, order-abc-123 | Check format, not exact value |
| **Timestamps** | 2024-03-14T10:30:45Z | Verify recent, valid format |
| **Random Values** | session tokens, nonces | Verify length, character set |
| **Sequential Numbers** | transaction IDs | Verify increasing, within range |
| **Calculated Fields** | totals with tax | Verify calculation logic |
| **Conditional Fields** | fields present only in some cases | Verify presence based on conditions |

