        metadata: {
            created: new Date().toISOString(),
            source: 'generated'
        }
    };
}
```

**10. Dynamic Data Best Practices**

✅ **Use unique data** – Prevent test collisions with timestamps or UUIDs
✅ **Realistic data** – Match production patterns for better test coverage
✅ **Boundary values** – Test edge cases (min, max, null, empty)
✅ **Clean up** – Delete generated test data after test execution
✅ **Reproducible** – Use seeds for random data to reproduce failures
✅ **Performance** – Generate efficiently for large datasets
✅ **Documentation** – Document data generation logic for maintainability
✅ **Validation** – Validate generated data before using
✅ **Separation** – Keep generation logic separate from test logic
✅ **Reusability** – Create shared data generation libraries

**11. Complete Example**

