**Finding and Manipulating Page Elements:**

**1. Locator Strategies**

```java
// By ID - fastest and most reliable
driver.findElement(By.id("username"));

// By Name - good for form fields
driver.findElement(By.name("password"));

// By Class Name - use with caution (can be duplicate)
driver.findElement(By.className("login-button"));

// By Tag Name - for collecting elements by HTML tag
driver.findElement(By.tagName("button"));

// By Link Text - for exact link text
driver.findElement(By.linkText("Click Here"));

// By Partial Link Text - for partial link text
driver.findElement(By.partialLinkText("Click"));

// By XPath - powerful but can be brittle
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//button[@id='submit']"));

// By CSS Selector - fast and flexible
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("#submit"));
```

**2. Finding Multiple Elements**

```java
// Returns list of matching elements
List<WebElement> buttons = driver.findElements(By.className("btn"));
System.out.println("Found " + buttons.size() + " buttons");

for (WebElement button : buttons) {
    System.out.println(button.getText());
}
```

**3. Element Actions**

```java
// Typing
WebElement input = driver.findElement(By.id("username"));
input.sendKeys("testuser");
input.clear();

// Clicking
WebElement button = driver.findElement(By.id("login"));
button.click();

// Getting text
String text = driver.findElement(By.className("welcome")).getText();

// Getting attributes
String href = driver.findElement(By.linkText("Home")).getAttribute("href");
String cssValue = driver.findElement(By.id("element")).getCssValue("color");

// Check state
boolean isDisplayed = driver.findElement(By.id("loading")).isDisplayed();
boolean isEnabled = driver.findElement(By.id("submit")).isEnabled();
boolean isSelected = driver.findElement(By.id("checkbox")).isSelected();
```

**4. Forms and Dropdowns**

```java
// Form submission
driver.findElement(By.id("search")).sendKeys("query");
driver.findElement(By.id("search")).submit(); // submits parent form

// Working with Select dropdowns
Select dropdown = new Select(driver.findElement(By.id("country")));
dropdown.selectByVisibleText("United States");
dropdown.selectByValue("us");
dropdown.selectByIndex(1);

// Get all options
List<WebElement> options = dropdown.getOptions();
```

**5. Checkboxes and Radio Buttons**

```java
// Checkbox
WebElement checkbox = driver.findElement(By.id("agree"));
if (!checkbox.isSelected()) {
    checkbox.click();
}

// Radio buttons
List<WebElement> radios = driver.findElements(By.name("gender"));
for (WebElement radio : radios) {
    if (radio.getAttribute("value").equals("female")) {
        radio.click();
        break;
    }
}
```

**6. Element Locator Priority**

```
✅ ID – Best (unique, fast)
✅ Name – Good (often unique)
✅ CSS Selector – Good (fast, flexible)
✅ XPath – Use when others fail
❌ Link Text – Only for links
❌ Class Name – Avoid if not unique
❌ Tag Name – Too broad
```

**7. Chaining Find Operations**

```java
// Find element within another element
