**8. Parallel Execution Best Practices**

✅ Use unique test data – Avoid collisions with timestamps
✅ Isolate test data – Each thread should have its own data
✅ No shared state – Don't use static/global variables
✅ Thread-safe reporting – Use thread-safe logging
✅ Resource limits – Don't overwhelm the system
✅ Monitor performance – Watch for contention
✅ Gradual scaling – Start with fewer threads, increase
✅ Clean up – Proper teardown after each test

