**Transforming a Linear Recording into an Intelligent Program:**

A recorded script is linear: Step A, then Step B, then Step C. Real-world user behavior is rarely linear. Users may repeat actions, take different paths based on data, or handle unexpected server responses. To simulate this, you need loops and conditional logic.

**Implementing Conditional Logic:**

The `if-else` statement is your primary tool for creating branches in your script.

```c
// Example: Handling different responses after a login attempt
web_reg_save_param("LoginStatus",
    "LB=status": "\"",
    "RB=\"",
    LAST);

web_submit_data("login.php",
    "Action=https://example.com/login",
    ...
    LAST);

// Check the captured status and take different actions
if (strcmp(lr_eval_string("{LoginStatus}"), "success") == 0) {
    lr_output_message("Login successful. Proceeding to dashboard.");
    web_url("dashboard.php", ...);
} else {
    lr_output_message("Login failed. Status: %s", lr_eval_string("{LoginStatus}"));
    // Optionally, attempt login again with different credentials
    // Or fail the transaction
    lr_end_transaction("Login", LR_FAIL);
}
```

**Implementing Loops for Repetitive Actions:**

`for` and `while` loops are essential for simulating iterative behaviors, such as adding multiple items to a cart or browsing through multiple pages of search results.

- **`for` Loop:** Use when you know in advance how many times an action should repeat.

```c
// Example: Adding 5 different items to a shopping cart
int item_count;
char item_param[50];

for (item_count = 1; item_count <= 5; item_count++) {
    // Build the parameter name dynamically, e.g., "item_id_1", "item_id_2"
    sprintf(item_param, "{item_id_%d}", item_count);

    web_submit_data("AddToCart.php",
        "Action=https://example.com/cart/add",
        "Method=POST",
        "RecContentType=text/html",
        "Referer=https://example.com/products",
        "Mode=HTML",
        ITEMDATA,
        "Name=itemId", "Value=", item_param, ENDITEM,
        LAST);

    lr_output_message("Added item %s to cart.", lr_eval_string(item_param));
}
```

- **`while` Loop:** Use when you need to repeat an action until a certain condition is met, such as paging through search results until you find a specific product.

```c
// Example: Paging through search results until the desired product is found
int page = 1;
int found = 0;
char next_page_url[256];

while (found == 0) {
    lr_output_message("Searching page %d...", page);

    web_url("search_results.php",
        "URL=https://example.com/search?page={page}",
        ...
        LAST);

    web_reg_save_param("product_found",
        "LB=Product ID: ",
        "RB= ",
        "Ord=All",
        LAST);

    // Check if the target product is on this page (logic to examine product_found array)
    // ... (omitted for brevity) ...

    if (/* product found */) {
        found = 1;
        lr_output_message("Product found on page %d.", page);
    } else {
        // Check if there is a "Next Page" link
        web_reg_save_param("next_link",
            "LB=<a href=\"",
            "RB=\" class=\"next\">",
            LAST);

        if (strlen(lr_eval_string("{next_link}")) == 0) {
            lr_output_message("No more pages. Product not found.");
            found = -1; // Exit loop, product not found
        } else {
            page++;
            lr_output_message("Going to next page.");
        }
    }
}
```

