**Example 5: DataProvider with Method Parameter**

You can pass the test method to the DataProvider for dynamic data generation.

```java
public class MethodAwareDataProviderTest {

    @DataProvider(name = "methodAware")
    public Object[][] provideData(Method method) {
        System.out.println("Providing data for method: " + method.getName());

        if (method.getName().equals("testLogin")) {
            return new Object[][]{
                {"user1", "pass1"},
                {"user2", "pass2"}
            };
        } else if (method.getName().equals("testRegistration")) {
            return new Object[][]{
                {"newuser1", "pass1", "user1@test.com"},
                {"newuser2", "pass2", "user2@test.com"}
            };
        }
        return new Object[0][0];
    }

    @Test(dataProvider = "methodAware")
    public void testLogin(String username, String password) {
        System.out.println("Testing login: " + username);
    }

    @Test(dataProvider = "methodAware")
    public void testRegistration(String username, String password, String email) {
        System.out.println("Testing registration: " + username + ", " + email);
    }
}
```

