**Key Assertion Patterns in This Example:**

| Pattern | Example | Purpose |
|---------|---------|---------|
| **Null Checks** | `Assert.assertNotNull(registeredUser.getId())` | Verify required fields exist |
| **Value Equality** | `Assert.assertEquals(user.getEmail(), email)` | Verify data was saved correctly |
| **Range Checks** | `Assert.assertTrue(duration < 500)` | Performance validation |
| **Collection Content** | `Assert.assertTrue(results.contains(product))` | Verify items in collections |
| **Exception Validation** | `Assert.assertEquals(e.getMessage(), expected)` | Verify error handling |
| **State Transitions** | `Assert.assertEquals(order.getStatus(), OrderStatus.PENDING)` | Verify business rules |
| **Mathematical Accuracy** | `Assert.assertEquals(total, expected, 0.01)` | Handle floating point precision |
| **Business Rules** | `Assert.assertFalse(user.isAdmin())` | Verify default user permissions |

content.explanation:
**The Problem with Hard Assertions:**

Standard TestNG assertions are "hard" assertions—when one fails, the test stops immediately. This can be inefficient when you want to validate multiple conditions in one test.

```java
@Test
public void testWithHardAssertions() {
    User user = userService.getUser(123);

    // If this fails, the test stops here
    Assert.assertNotNull(user, "User should exist");

    // These assertions won't run if user is null
    Assert.assertEquals(user.getName(), "John Doe");
    Assert.assertEquals(user.getEmail(), "john@test.com");
    Assert.assertTrue(user.isActive());
}
```

**Soft Assertions to the Rescue:**

Soft assertions collect all assertion failures and report them at the end, allowing multiple validations in one test.

```java
import org.testng.asserts.SoftAssert;

public class SoftAssertionsTest {

    @Test
    public void testWithSoftAssertions() {
        SoftAssert softAssert = new SoftAssert();

        User user = userService.getUser(123);

        // All assertions run even if some fail
        softAssert.assertNotNull(user, "User should exist");

        // These will run even if user is null (but will cause NPE)
        // Better to check null first with hard assertion or conditional
        if (user != null) {
            softAssert.assertEquals(user.getName(), "John Doe", "Name check");
            softAssert.assertEquals(user.getEmail(), "john@test.com", "Email check");
            softAssert.assertTrue(user.isActive(), "Active status check");
            softAssert.assertEquals(user.getAge(), 30, "Age check");
        }

        // Don't forget this! It reports all failures at the end
        softAssert.assertAll();
    }
}
```

**Real-World Soft Assertion Example:**

```java
public class UserProfileSoftAssertTest {

    @Test
    public void testUserProfileCompleteness() {
        SoftAssert softAssert = new SoftAssert();

        // Get user profile with multiple fields to validate
        UserProfile profile = userService.getUserProfile(123);

        // Required fields - these must exist
        softAssert.assertNotNull(profile, "Profile should exist");

        if (profile != null) {
            // Basic info validation
            softAssert.assertNotNull(profile.getUserId(), "User ID required");
            softAssert.assertNotNull(profile.getUsername(), "Username required");
            softAssert.assertNotNull(profile.getEmail(), "Email required");

            // Optional fields - validate format if present
            if (profile.getPhone() != null) {
                softAssert.assertTrue(
                    profile.getPhone().matches("\\d{10}"),
                    "Phone should be 10 digits"
                );
            }

            if (profile.getBirthDate() != null) {
                softAssert.assertTrue(
                    profile.getBirthDate().before(new Date()),
                    "Birth date should be in past"
                );

                // Calculate age from birth date
                int age = calculateAge(profile.getBirthDate());
                softAssert.assertTrue(
                    age >= 18 && age <= 120,
                    "Age should be between 18 and 120"
                );
            }

            // Address validation
            Address address = profile.getAddress();
            softAssert.assertNotNull(address, "Address should exist");

            if (address != null) {
                softAssert.assertNotNull(address.getStreet(), "Street required");
                softAssert.assertNotNull(address.getCity(), "City required");
                softAssert.assertNotNull(address.getZipCode(), "Zip code required");

                if (address.getZipCode() != null) {
                    softAssert.assertTrue(
                        address.getZipCode().matches("\\d{5}"),
                        "Zip code should be 5 digits"
                    );
                }
            }

            // Preferences validation
            UserPreferences prefs = profile.getPreferences();
            softAssert.assertNotNull(prefs, "Preferences should exist");

            if (prefs != null) {
                softAssert.assertNotNull(prefs.getLanguage(), "Language preference required");
                softAssert.assertNotNull(prefs.getCurrency(), "Currency preference required");

                // Validate email notifications flag
                softAssert.assertNotNull(prefs.isEmailNotifications(), 
                    "Email notifications flag required");
            }
        }

        // Report all failures
        softAssert.assertAll();
    }
}
```

**Soft Assertions with Custom Messages and Grouping:**

