</suite>
```

**8. Parallel Execution with Retry**

```java
public class RetryAnalyzer implements IRetryAnalyzer {
    private int retryCount = 0;
    private static final int MAX_RETRY = 2;

    @Override
    public boolean retry(ITestResult result) {
        if (retryCount < MAX_RETRY) {
            retryCount++;
            System.out.printf("Retrying test %s in thread %d (attempt %d)%n",
                result.getName(),
                Thread.currentThread().getId(),
                retryCount);
            return true;
        }
        return false;
    }
}

public class RetryTest {
    @Test(retryAnalyzer = RetryAnalyzer.class)
    public void testFlaky() {
        // Test that may fail intermittently
    }
}
```

**9. Debugging Parallel Execution**

```java
public class ParallelDebugger {

    public static void printThreadDump() {
        Map<Thread, StackTraceElement[]> threadDumps = Thread.getAllStackTraces();

        System.out.println("=== Thread Dump ===");
        for (Map.Entry<Thread, StackTraceElement[]> entry : threadDumps.entrySet()) {
            Thread thread = entry.getKey();
            System.out.printf("Thread: %s (ID: %d, State: %s)%n",
                thread.getName(), thread.getId(), thread.getState());

            for (StackTraceElement element : entry.getValue()) {
                System.out.println("  at " + element);
            }
        }
    }

    public static void monitorThreads() {
        ScheduledExecutorService scheduler = Executors.newScheduledThreadPool(1);
        scheduler.scheduleAtFixedRate(() -> {
            int activeThreads = Thread.activeCount();
            System.out.printf("Active threads: %d%n", activeThreads);

            if (activeThreads > 50) {
                System.out.println("⚠️ High thread count detected!");
                printThreadDump();
            }
        }, 0, 10, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
    }
}
```

**10. Common Parallel Execution Pitfalls**

| Pitfall | Symptom | Solution |
|---------|---------|----------|
| **Static variables** | Tests interfere, non-deterministic failures | Use ThreadLocal, avoid static state |
| **Shared test data** | Tests fail intermittently | Unique data per thread, transactions |
| **Too many threads** | Slowdown due to context switching | Monitor performance, adjust thread count |
| **Resource exhaustion** | OutOfMemoryError, connection timeouts | Pool resources, limit concurrent usage |
| **Deadlocks** | Tests hang indefinitely | Review synchronization, use timeouts |
| **Log file corruption** | Interleaved log messages | Use thread-aware logging |
| **Race conditions** | Tests pass/fail inconsistently | Synchronize critical sections, use atomic variables |
| **Thread leak** | Thread count grows over time | Ensure threads are cleaned up in @AfterMethod |

