**13. Performance Metrics**

```java
// Track test execution time in CI
public class PerformanceTracker {
    private static final Map<String, List<Long>> testTimes = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    @Override
    public void onTestSuccess(ITestResult result) {
        long duration = result.getEndMillis() - result.getStartMillis();
        String testName = result.getName();

        testTimes.computeIfAbsent(testName, k -> new ArrayList<>()).add(duration);

        // Alert if test is slowing down
        if (duration > 5000) {
            System.out.println("⚠️ Slow test: " + testName + " took " + duration + "ms");
        }
    }

    @AfterSuite
    public void reportPerformance() {
        // Generate performance trend report
        for (Map.Entry<String, List<Long>> entry : testTimes.entrySet()) {
            List<Long> times = entry.getValue();
            double avg = times.stream().mapToLong(Long::longValue).average().orElse(0);
            System.out.printf("%s: avg=%.2fms, runs=%d%n", 
                entry.getKey(), avg, times.size());
        }
    }
}
```

**14. Common Pitfalls to Avoid**

| Pitfall | Solution |
|---------|----------|
